# ARR! DB Types: UUIDs vs Strings for IDs and Foreign Keys

## Policy
- All ID columns and foreign keys in this codebase are `sa.String()` (VARCHAR), not native UUID.
- Always cast `uuid.UUID` objects to `str()` before passing to queries.
- Validate UUIDs at the API/model layer to avoid storing garbage.

## Rationale
- Native UUID columns and FKs cause trouble with migrations, drivers, and test data.
- Mixing types (UUID in one table, String in another) breaks foreign keys and migrations.
- String columns work everywhere, but ye lose strict type safety.

## Migration Advice
- If ye ever want to switch to native UUIDs, plan a full migration:
  - Update all models and migrations to use `sa.UUID(as_uuid=True)`.
  - Update all code and test data to use `uuid.UUID` objects.
  - Run a one-time migration to convert all string UUIDs to native UUIDs.
- Do it all at once, or not at all!

